---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="How to Become a Tree Billionaire in 5 Years">
    
  <div class="relative h-80 md:h-[420px] overflow-hidden">
    <img src="/blog_tree.png" alt="Tree Billionaire" class="w-full h-full object-cover"/>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/70 via-black/30 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 p-8 md:p-16 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <span class="inline-block bg-emerald-600 text-white text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Forestry & Climate</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white leading-tight">How to Become a Tree Billionaire in 5 Years</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Main Layout Section with Sidebar -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-14">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
      
      <!-- Left Column: The Article Content -->
      <article class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-8">
        <!-- Meta -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500 mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-gray-200">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] text-primary">calendar_today</span> Jun 02, 2026</div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] text-primary">person</span> Tree Billionaires Team</div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] text-primary">schedule</span> 7 min read</div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] text-primary">visibility</span> <span id="view-count-text">Loading views...</span></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Body -->
        <div class="prose max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 font-medium leading-relaxed">What if every farmer, every schoolchild, every community had access to a living investment that grew in value every single year — one that also healed the planet? That is the simple, powerful premise behind the Bill of Senga's Tree Billionaire Generation program.</p>

          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-secondary mt-10">The Vision: A Billion Trees, A Billion Futures</h2>
          <p>The name "Tree Billionaire" does not refer to money in the traditional sense — though trees do generate enormous economic value. It refers to a state of ecological and community wealth: the richness of a landscape where a billion indigenous trees shade homes, hold soil, filter water, and feed families. A Tree Billionaire is someone who has made a generational commitment to planting, nurturing, and stewarding trees as a long-term living investment.</p>

          <p>Our program targets youth, smallholder farmers, and women's groups across East and Central Africa. We provide free indigenous tree seedlings, training in agroforestry techniques, and a mobile monitoring system to track tree survival and growth. Participants earn micro-rewards for every verified tree that reaches 6 months of age.</p>

          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-secondary mt-10">Why Indigenous Trees?</h2>
          <p>Not all trees are equal. Exotic fast-growing species like eucalyptus and pine — widely planted in reforestation programs — actually degrade biodiversity and drain local water tables. They offer carbon sequestration but destroy the ecological communities that indigenous forests support.</p>
          <p>BOS exclusively promotes native species: Acacia, Markhamia, Warburgia, Prunus africana, and dozens more. These trees evolved with local insects, birds, and soil communities over millennia. They provide:</p>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-3 mt-4">
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span><span><strong>Food security</strong> — fruit, leaves, and seeds used in traditional diets</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span><span><strong>Medicinal value</strong> — bark and roots used in traditional healthcare for generations</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span><span><strong>Timber and fuel</strong> — sustainably harvested without destroying the tree</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span><span><strong>Soil restoration</strong> — deep root systems break hardpan layers and channel rainwater underground</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span><span><strong>Carbon locking</strong> — long-lived indigenous species store more carbon per tree than short-rotation crops</span></li>
          </ul>

          <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-emerald-600 pl-6 py-2 bg-emerald-50 rounded-r-xl my-8">
            <p class="text-lg italic text-secondary font-medium">"My grandfather planted three Warburgia trees before I was born. I still harvest their bark for medicine today. When I plant 200 trees this season, I am writing a letter to my grandchildren."</p>
            <cite class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 block">— Julius Katende, Tree Billionaire Participant, Uganda</cite>
          </blockquote>

          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-secondary mt-10">Your 5-Year Tree Billionaire Roadmap</h2>
          <div class="space-y-5 mt-4">
            <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 bg-surface-container-low rounded-xl border border-outline-variant">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-display font-bold text-lg">Y1</div>
              <div><strong class="text-secondary block mb-1">Start small, start right:</strong> Plant 50–100 seedlings on your homestead and farm boundaries. Focus on soil preparation, mulching, and watering discipline in the first dry season. Survival rate target: 80%.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 bg-surface-container-low rounded-xl border border-outline-variant">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-display font-bold text-lg">Y2</div>
              <div><strong class="text-secondary block mb-1">Expand and train:</strong> Recruit two neighbouring farmers. Together, plant another 300 trees. Share maintenance knowledge and begin keeping a tree journal — recording species, location, height progress.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 bg-surface-container-low rounded-xl border border-outline-variant">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-display font-bold text-lg">Y3</div>
              <div><strong class="text-secondary block mb-1">Start a community nursery:</strong> Produce your own seedlings from seeds collected locally. A community nursery of 500–1,000 seedlings per season makes you a regional supplier, generating income while planting more trees.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 bg-surface-container-low rounded-xl border border-outline-variant">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-display font-bold text-lg">Y5</div>
              <div><strong class="text-secondary block mb-1">Become a Tree Billionaire Ambassador:</strong> You now have a living forest of 1,000+ trees. You are generating ecosystem services — shade, clean water, soil stability — and economic value from sustainable harvest of fruits, bark, and seeds. You join BOS as a certified ambassador.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-secondary mt-10">How to Get Started with BOS</h2>
          <p>The Tree Billionaire Generation program accepts new cohorts every quarter. Joining gives you access to free indigenous seedlings, field training from BOS agroforestry experts, a mobile app for monitoring your trees, micro-rewards for verified survival milestones, and a network of fellow Tree Billionaires across Africa.</p>
          <p>Visit our <a href="/tree_billionaire_generation/" class="text-primary font-semibold underline underline-offset-2">Tree Billionaires Hub</a> to learn more, or sign up at our next Practical Classroom session. The forest of tomorrow begins with the seed you plant today.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Tags -->
        <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-surface-container-low text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600 rounded-full border border-gray-200">Reforestation</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-surface-container-low text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600 rounded-full border border-gray-200">Agroforestry</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-surface-container-low text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600 rounded-full border border-gray-200">Climate Action</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-surface-container-low text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600 rounded-full border border-gray-200">Indigenous Species</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Comments Section -->
        <div class="mt-12 pt-10 border-t border-gray-200" id="comments-section">
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-secondary mb-6">Join the Discussion</h3>
          
          <!-- Comment Form -->
          <form id="comment-form" class="mb-10 bg-surface-container-low p-6 rounded-2xl border border-outline-variant">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-1">Name</label>
                <input type="text" id="comment-name" required class="w-full px-4 py-2 rounded-xl border border-gray-300 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary focus:ring-1 focus:ring-primary" placeholder="Your name">
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-1">Email <span class="text-gray-400 font-normal">(Optional)</span></label>
                <input type="email" id="comment-email" class="w-full px-4 py-2 rounded-xl border border-gray-300 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary focus:ring-1 focus:ring-primary" placeholder="Your email">
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-4">
              <label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-1">Comment</label>
              <textarea id="comment-body" required rows="4" class="w-full px-4 py-2 rounded-xl border border-gray-300 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary focus:ring-1 focus:ring-primary" placeholder="Share your thoughts..."></textarea>
            </div>
            <button type="submit" class="bg-primary hover:bg-[#002b54] text-white px-6 py-2.5 rounded-full font-semibold transition-colors">
              Post Comment
            </button>
          </form>

          <!-- Comments List -->
          <div id="comments-list" class="space-y-6">
            <!-- Comments will be rendered here via JS -->
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Related / Back -->
        <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
          <a href="/blog/post-1-healthy-soil.html" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-semibold hover:gap-3 transition-all text-sm">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px]">arrow_back</span> Previous Post
          </a>
          <a href="/blog/post-3-urban-rooftop.html" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-semibold hover:gap-3 transition-all text-sm">
            Next Post <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px]">arrow_forward</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Right Column: Sidebar -->
      <aside class="lg:col-span-4 space-y-8">
        
        <!-- Search Box -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 shadow-md border border-gray-100/80">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-secondary mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">search</span>
            Search Blog
          </h3>
          <div class="relative font-body">
            <input type="text" id="sidebar-search-input" onkeyup="window.location.href='/blog/?q='+this.value" placeholder="Type keywords..." class="w-full pl-4 pr-10 py-3 bg-stone-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl focus:outline-none focus:border-primary focus:ring-1 focus:ring-primary text-sm transition-all"/>
            <span class="absolute right-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-gray-400 material-symbols-outlined text-[18px]">search</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Categories Widget -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 shadow-md border border-gray-100/80">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-secondary mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">category</span>
            Categories
          </h3>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 font-label-md" id="sidebar-categories-list">
            <!-- Dynamically computed categories -->
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Popular Posts Widget -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 shadow-md border border-gray-100/80">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-secondary mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">trending_up</span>
            Popular Articles
          </h3>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4" id="sidebar-popular-posts">
            <!-- Dynamically listed popular posts -->
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Join the Movement CTA -->
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-secondary via-[#1a3525] to-[#003B73] rounded-3xl p-6 shadow-md text-white border border-gray-100/10 relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute -right-8 -bottom-8 w-24 h-24 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10"></div>
          <p class="text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Sustainable Living</p>
          <h3 class="font-display text-base font-bold mb-3 leading-snug">Ready to start your green journey?</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-300 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-5 font-body">Access micro-gardening guides, local seed swaps, and expert-led webinars in our premium community forum.</p>
          <a href="/join_the_movement/" class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center bg-gradient-to-r from-primary to-[#0052a3] text-white py-3 rounded-full font-semibold text-xs hover:shadow-lg hover:shadow-primary/20 transition-all gap-1.5 border-b-2 border-emerald-400">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">forum</span>
            Join the Movement
          </a>
        </div>

      </aside>

    </div>
  </section>

    
<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const postId = window.location.pathname.split('/').pop().replace('.html', '') || 'post';
    const form = document.getElementById('comment-form');
    const nameInput = document.getElementById('comment-name');
    const bodyInput = document.getElementById('comment-body');
    const commentsList = document.getElementById('comments-list');

    const defaultComments = [
      { id: 1, name: "David M.", date: "1 day ago", body: "I started planting Warburgia trees last year based on this approach. The survival rate is amazing when you use indigenous species.", avatar: "DM" },
      { id: 2, name: "Alice N.", date: "5 hours ago", body: "The concept of 'Tree Billionaires' is exactly what we need to inspire the youth. Great read!", avatar: "AN" }
    ];

    function loadComments() {
      const stored = localStorage.getItem(`bos_comments_${postId}`);
      if (stored) return JSON.parse(stored);
      localStorage.setItem(`bos_comments_${postId}`, JSON.stringify(defaultComments));
      return defaultComments;
    }

    function saveComments(comments) {
      localStorage.setItem(`bos_comments_${postId}`, JSON.stringify(comments));
    }

    function renderComments() {
      const comments = loadComments();
      if (comments.length === 0) {
        commentsList.innerHTML = `<p class="text-gray-500 italic">No comments yet. Be the first to share your thoughts!</p>`;
        return;
      }

      commentsList.innerHTML = comments.map(c => `
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold flex-shrink-0">
            ${c.avatar}
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900">${c.name}</h4>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-400">${c.date}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">${c.body}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      `).join('');
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const name = nameInput.value.trim();
      const body = bodyInput.value.trim();
      if (!name || !body) return;

      const newComment = {
        id: Date.now(),
        name: name,
        date: "Just now",
        body: body,
        avatar: name.substring(0, 2).toUpperCase()
      };

      const comments = loadComments();
      comments.unshift(newComment);
      saveComments(comments);
      
      renderComments();
      form.reset();
    });

    renderComments();

    // Views count logic
    const viewsKey = `bos_views_${postId}`;
    const initialViews = 89;
    let currentViews = parseInt(localStorage.getItem(viewsKey));
    if (isNaN(currentViews)) {
      currentViews = initialViews;
    }
    
    // Add 1 view on load
    currentViews += 1;
    localStorage.setItem(viewsKey, currentViews);
    
    const viewsTextEl = document.getElementById('view-count-text');
    if (viewsTextEl) {
      viewsTextEl.innerText = `${currentViews.toLocaleString()} views`;
    }

    // Sidebar Dynamic Renderers
    function renderSidebar() {
      // 1. Categories counting
      const categoriesListEl = document.getElementById('sidebar-categories-list');
      if (categoriesListEl) {
        const allPosts = [
          { category: 'Soil Science' },
          { category: 'Forestry & Climate' },
          { category: 'Urban Farming' }
        ];

        // Load custom ones
        const customPosts = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('bos_custom_posts') || '[]');
        customPosts.forEach(cp => {
          if (cp.status === 'published' && new Date(cp.publishDate || cp.createdAt) <= new Date()) {
            allPosts.push(cp);
          }
        });

        const counts = {};
        allPosts.forEach(p => {
          counts[p.category] = (counts[p.category] || 0) + 1;
        });

        categoriesListEl.innerHTML = Object.entries(counts).map(([cat, count]) => `
          <a href="/blog/?category=${encodeURIComponent(cat)}" class="flex justify-between items-center px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl hover:bg-stone-50 text-stone-600 hover:text-primary transition-all">
            <span>${cat}</span>
            <span class="bg-stone-100 text-stone-500 text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full font-bold">${count}</span>
          </a>
        `).join('');
      }

      // 2. Popular posts sorting & listing
      const popularPostsEl = document.getElementById('sidebar-popular-posts');
      if (popularPostsEl) {
        const nativePopular = [
          { id: 'post-1-healthy-soil', title: 'From "Hell" to a Living Laboratory', img: '/blog_soil.png', date: 'May 15, 2026', initial: 142 },
          { id: 'post-2-tree-billionaire', title: 'Become a Tree Billionaire in 5 Years', img: '/blog_tree.png', date: 'Jun 02, 2026', initial: 89 },
          { id: 'post-3-urban-rooftop', title: 'Urban Rooftop Farming: Feeding Cities', img: '/blog_rooftop.png', date: 'Jun 20, 2026', initial: 64 }
        ];

        const mergedPopular = nativePopular.map(np => {
          const vKey = `bos_views_${np.id}`;
          let viewsVal = parseInt(localStorage.getItem(vKey)) || np.initial;
          return { ...np, views: viewsVal, link: `/blog/${np.id}.html` };
        });

        // Add custom published ones
        const customPosts = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('bos_custom_posts') || '[]');
        customPosts.forEach(cp => {
          if (cp.status === 'published' && new Date(cp.publishDate || cp.createdAt) <= new Date()) {
            const vKey = `bos_views_${cp.id}`;
            let viewsVal = parseInt(localStorage.getItem(vKey)) || cp.initialViews || 42;
            mergedPopular.push({
              id: cp.id,
              title: cp.title,
              img: cp.featuredImage || '/blog_soil.png',
              date: formatDate(cp.publishDate || cp.createdAt),
              views: viewsVal,
              link: `/blog/view.html?id=${cp.id}`
            });
          }
        });

        // Sort
        mergedPopular.sort((a, b) => b.views - a.views);

        // Slice top 3
        const top3 = mergedPopular.slice(0, 3);

        popularPostsEl.innerHTML = top3.map(postItem => `
          <a href="${postItem.link}" class="flex gap-3 group">
            <img src="${postItem.img}" alt="" class="w-16 h-16 object-cover rounded-xl flex-shrink-0 group-hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity border border-gray-100"/>
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-display text-sm font-semibold text-secondary group-hover:text-primary transition-colors line-clamp-2 leading-snug">${postItem.title}</h4>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] text-gray-400 mt-1">
                <span>${postItem.date}</span>
                <span>•</span>
                <span class="flex items-center gap-0.5"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[12px] text-primary">visibility</span> <span class="pop-views-${postItem.id}">${postItem.views.toLocaleString()} views</span></span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </a>
        `).join('');
      }
    }

    function formatDate(dateStr) {
      if (!dateStr) return '';
      try {
        const d = new Date(dateStr);
        const months = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];
        return `${months[d.getMonth()]} ${String(d.getDate()).padStart(2, '0')}, ${d.getFullYear()}`;
      } catch (e) {
        return dateStr;
      }
    }

    // Run initial sync
    renderSidebar();

    // Every 3 minutes (180,000 ms), add 5 views
    setInterval(() => {
      currentViews += 5;
      localStorage.setItem(viewsKey, currentViews);
      if (viewsTextEl) {
        viewsTextEl.innerText = `${currentViews.toLocaleString()} views`;
      }
      renderSidebar();
    }, 180000);
  });
</script>
</Layout>
